"""scripts/experiment.py - THIS campaign's code: the five experiment hooks and the optional seams.

The one script a campaign edits. scripts/run_campaign.py is the kit's machinery (the gates, the checks,
the snapshot, the driver, the prompts): it calls the functions below and is replaced wholesale on a kit
upgrade - never edit it per campaign. Everything the runner records about an experiment comes from
these hooks; everything it needs from the campaign, it asks for here.

Required (preflight refuses to launch while any is still a stub):
  validate_method(cfg)                 hard-fail on a lever value nothing dispatches on
  run_experiment(cfg) -> prediction    the levers live here, dispatched on the config
  load_target(cfg) -> target           what the FROZEN metric scores against
Called every experiment (working stubs below; make them real):
  guardrail(prediction, cfg) -> dict   the co-tracked diagnostic ({{GUARDRAIL_METRIC}}); logged, not primary
  save_figure(label, prediction, target, residual) -> Path
Optional seams (define one to extend the record; omit it and the runner uses its default):
  residual(prediction, target)                        what save_figure's residual panel shows (None = none)
  campaign_scoreboard_fields(cfg, diags, score) -> dict   extra scoreboard columns (levers, diagnostics, run numerics)
  campaign_checks(exp_id, label, score, diags, cfg) -> dict   name -> {"status": "pass"|"fail"|"unavailable", "detail": ...}
  campaign_card_fields(result, checks) -> dict        extra lines of the result card (name -> value): the
                                                      campaign's own comparison numbers the analysis needs
  baseline_config() -> dict                           the exp 000 config that `--baseline` runs
Helpers this campaign needs (a forward model, a fitter, a data reader) live here or in sibling modules
you add to scripts/; the per-experiment snapshot copies the whole directory, so every run stays
reproducible after later edits.
"""
